{
  "$comment": [
    "Seed catalogue. `npm run seed` upserts this into SQLite (safe to re-run).",
    "A part can have several listings; the tracker records a price per (part, retailer)",
    "and shows the cheapest one. ASINs are only filled in where they were supplied —",
    "no ASIN is guessed. A listing without an ASIN carries a `query` instead: search-capable",
    "sources match on it, and its link resolves to an Amazon search rather than a product",
    "page, because those parts were specified by class rather than by exact SKU.",
    "`url` is derived at seed time when omitted; set it explicitly to override.",
    "`allowHtml` / `allowBrowser` opt a single listing into the robots.txt-checked sources."
  ],
